# scoursh CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark control labels - rules/RULE-FORMAT.md
# §9.6.7.  Normative document: docs/CIS-MAPPINGS.md - read it before adding,
# editing, or refreshing a row here.
#
# COMPLIANCE-03 (docs/STEP10-SARIF-PLAN.md Track B): an id -> LABEL reference
# table, never a source of control ids.  A check's `cis:` field (§9.1, §9.2,
# §9.5) is authored on the check record itself; this file only expands a
# control id already on a finding into its published short title, exactly as
# data/owasp-categories.conf expands an `owasp` id (§9.6.6, COMPLIANCE-01).
#
# Benchmark: CIS Amazon Web Services Foundations Benchmark
# Version:   3.0.0
#
# "CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark v3.0.0 control 1.4" and "v1.4.0 control 1.4"
# are different controls (the captain's D4 decision,
# docs/STEP10-SARIF-PLAN.md's own COMPLIANCE-03 row), so the benchmark name
# and version are carried as DATA on the first record below (`benchmark`,
# `benchmark-version`), not only in this header comment - every CLOUD-*/
# POSTURE-* check that cites a `cis:` value cites one against v3.0.0.
#
# Copyright-safe by construction (D4): this file transcribes CONTROL IDS and
# their PUBLISHED SHORT TITLES only, never the benchmark's rationale, audit,
# or remediation prose, which is CIS's copyrighted content - the schema
# (§9.6.7) has no field for any of that prose.
#
# A SEED, not the whole benchmark: docs/DESIGN.md §3's own AWS-service table
# uses the identical phrase for the identical reason.  This covers 34
# controls across the v1(CIS-core) service scope - IAM, S3, EC2/VPC - plus
# the logging/monitoring controls (CloudTrail, AWS Config, KMS, EFS, RDS)
# that scope's own checks also cite, cross-referenced against AWS Security
# Hub's own public CIS v3.0.0 control-id mapping
# (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/cis-aws-foundations-benchmark.html),
# which republishes CIS control numbers alongside its own control titles as
# part of its own standards documentation.  Section 4 (the CloudWatch
# metric-filter/alarm controls) is NOT transcribed: Security Hub's own
# mapping marks every one of those "Not supported - manual check" for
# v3.0.0 and does not name their v3.0.0 control numbers, so this file cannot
# cite them without the source PDF in hand.  docs/CIS-MAPPINGS.md §5 (the
# refresh procedure) is how that gap - and any control this table has not
# yet been given a row for - gets closed.
#
# `benchmark`, `benchmark-version`, and `format-version` are meaningful only
# on the FIRST record, exactly as data/owasp-categories.conf's
# `format-version` is (rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9.6.6) - repeating them on every
# record would only give a future benchmark-version bump a second place to
# edit.

